{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000107",
  "title": "N-Body Gravity Simulation",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[dependencies]\nplotters = \"0.3\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "shared_source": null,
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "> *AI authored to showcase ironpad capabilities.*\n\n# N-Body Gravity Simulation 🪐\n\nThe **N-body problem** asks: given $N$ massive bodies interacting through gravity, how do they move over time?\n\n## The Physics\n\nNewton's law of gravitation gives the force between two bodies:\n\n$$F = \\frac{G \\, m_1 \\, m_2}{r^2}$$\n\nFor $N$ bodies, each feels the combined gravitational pull of every other body — requiring $\\binom{N}{2} = N(N\\!-\\!1)/2$ force pair calculations per timestep.\n\n## Our Approach\n\nWe simulate a **central star** (mass $= 200$) with **four orbiting planets** using **Velocity Verlet integration** — a symplectic integrator that conserves energy far better than naive Euler methods. A softening parameter $\\varepsilon$ prevents numerical singularities at close approach.\n\nRun the cells below to see orbital mechanics emerge from simple force laws!",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "N-Body Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// N-Body gravitational simulation using Velocity Verlet integration\n\nlet g = 1.0_f64;\nlet dt = 0.01_f64;\nlet steps = 2000_usize;\nlet eps = 0.1_f64;\n\n// Body state arrays: positions, velocities, and masses\n// Central star + 4 planets at increasing orbital radii\nlet mut x:  Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  5.0,  0.0, -12.0,   0.0];\nlet mut y:  Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  0.0,  8.0,   0.0, -16.0];\nlet mut vx: Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  0.0, -(g * 200.0 / 8.0_f64).sqrt(),  0.0, (g * 200.0 / 16.0_f64).sqrt()];\nlet mut vy: Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  (g * 200.0 / 5.0_f64).sqrt(), 0.0, -(g * 200.0 / 12.0_f64).sqrt(), 0.0];\nlet mass: Vec<f64>   = vec![200.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.5];\n\nlet n = mass.len();\n\n// Compute gravitational accelerations on each body\nfn accel(x: &[f64], y: &[f64], mass: &[f64], g: f64, eps: f64) -> (Vec<f64>, Vec<f64>) {\n    let n = mass.len();\n    let mut ax = vec![0.0; n];\n    let mut ay = vec![0.0; n];\n    for i in 0..n {\n        for j in (i + 1)..n {\n            let dx = x[j] - x[i];\n            let dy = y[j] - y[i];\n            let r2 = dx * dx + dy * dy + eps * eps;\n            let inv_r3 = 1.0 / (r2 * r2.sqrt());\n            // Force on i from j\n            ax[i] += g * mass[j] * dx * inv_r3;\n            ay[i] += g * mass[j] * dy * inv_r3;\n            // Newton's third law: equal and opposite on j\n            ax[j] -= g * mass[i] * dx * inv_r3;\n            ay[j] -= g * mass[i] * dy * inv_r3;\n        }\n    }\n    (ax, ay)\n}\n\n// Record position history (sampled every 10 steps for clean output)\nlet mut histories: Vec<Vec<(f64, f64)>> = (0..n)\n    .map(|i| vec![(x[i], y[i])])\n    .collect();\n\n// Velocity Verlet integration\nlet (mut ax, mut ay) = accel(&x, &y, &mass, g, eps);\n\nfor step in 1..=steps {\n    // Update positions: x += v*dt + 0.5*a*dt²\n    for i in 0..n {\n        x[i] += vx[i] * dt + 0.5 * ax[i] * dt * dt;\n        y[i] += vy[i] * dt + 0.5 * ay[i] * dt * dt;\n    }\n\n    // Compute new accelerations from updated positions\n    let (ax_new, ay_new) = accel(&x, &y, &mass, g, eps);\n\n    // Update velocities: v += 0.5*(a_old + a_new)*dt\n    for i in 0..n {\n        vx[i] += 0.5 * (ax[i] + ax_new[i]) * dt;\n        vy[i] += 0.5 * (ay[i] + ay_new[i]) * dt;\n    }\n\n    ax = ax_new;\n    ay = ay_new;\n\n    // Sample every 10th step to keep output manageable\n    if step % 10 == 0 {\n        for i in 0..n {\n            histories[i].push((x[i], y[i]));\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nCellOutput::text(format!(\n    \"Simulated {} bodies for {} steps (dt={}). {} points per body.\",\n    n, steps, dt, histories[0].len()\n))\n",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Text\":\"Simulated 5 bodies for 2000 steps (dt=0.01). 201 points per body.\"}]"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Orbital Trail Visualization",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Re-run the simulation to get full trajectory data for rendering\nlet g = 1.0_f64;\nlet dt = 0.01_f64;\nlet steps = 2000_usize;\nlet eps = 0.1_f64;\n\nlet mut x:  Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  5.0,  0.0, -12.0,   0.0];\nlet mut y:  Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  0.0,  8.0,   0.0, -16.0];\nlet mut vx: Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  0.0, -(g * 200.0 / 8.0_f64).sqrt(),  0.0, (g * 200.0 / 16.0_f64).sqrt()];\nlet mut vy: Vec<f64> = vec![ 0.0,  (g * 200.0 / 5.0_f64).sqrt(), 0.0, -(g * 200.0 / 12.0_f64).sqrt(), 0.0];\nlet mass: Vec<f64>   = vec![200.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.5];\nlet n = mass.len();\n\nfn accel(x: &[f64], y: &[f64], mass: &[f64], g: f64, eps: f64) -> (Vec<f64>, Vec<f64>) {\n    let n = mass.len();\n    let mut ax = vec![0.0; n];\n    let mut ay = vec![0.0; n];\n    for i in 0..n {\n        for j in (i + 1)..n {\n            let dx = x[j] - x[i];\n            let dy = y[j] - y[i];\n            let r2 = dx * dx + dy * dy + eps * eps;\n            let inv_r3 = 1.0 / (r2 * r2.sqrt());\n            ax[i] += g * mass[j] * dx * inv_r3;\n            ay[i] += g * mass[j] * dy * inv_r3;\n            ax[j] -= g * mass[i] * dx * inv_r3;\n            ay[j] -= g * mass[i] * dy * inv_r3;\n        }\n    }\n    (ax, ay)\n}\n\nlet mut histories: Vec<Vec<(f64, f64)>> = (0..n)\n    .map(|i| vec![(x[i], y[i])])\n    .collect();\n\nlet (mut ax, mut ay) = accel(&x, &y, &mass, g, eps);\nfor _ in 1..=steps {\n    for i in 0..n {\n        x[i] += vx[i] * dt + 0.5 * ax[i] * dt * dt;\n        y[i] += vy[i] * dt + 0.5 * ay[i] * dt * dt;\n    }\n    let (ax_new, ay_new) = accel(&x, &y, &mass, g, eps);\n    for i in 0..n {\n        vx[i] += 0.5 * (ax[i] + ax_new[i]) * dt;\n        vy[i] += 0.5 * (ay[i] + ay_new[i]) * dt;\n    }\n    ax = ax_new;\n    ay = ay_new;\n    for i in 0..n {\n        histories[i].push((x[i], y[i]));\n    }\n}\n\n// Find coordinate bounds for the plot\nlet (mut min_x, mut max_x) = (f64::MAX, f64::MIN);\nlet (mut min_y, mut max_y) = (f64::MAX, f64::MIN);\nfor traj in &histories {\n    for &(px, py) in traj {\n        min_x = min_x.min(px);\n        max_x = max_x.max(px);\n        min_y = min_y.min(py);\n        max_y = max_y.max(py);\n    }\n}\nlet pad = 2.0;\nmin_x -= pad; max_x += pad;\nmin_y -= pad; max_y += pad;\n\n// Body colors and labels\nlet colors = [\n    RGBColor(255, 220, 80),  // Star: golden\n    RGBColor(100, 180, 255), // Planet 1: blue\n    RGBColor(255, 100, 100), // Planet 2: red\n    RGBColor(100, 230, 150), // Planet 3: green\n    RGBColor(200, 140, 255), // Planet 4: purple\n];\nlet labels = [\"Star\", \"Inner\", \"Second\", \"Third\", \"Outer\"];\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (800, 800))\n        .into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&RGBColor(15, 15, 25)).unwrap();\n\n    let mut chart = ChartBuilder::on(&root)\n        .caption(\"N-Body Orbital Trails\", (\"sans-serif\", 22).into_font().color(&WHITE))\n        .margin(15)\n        .x_label_area_size(35)\n        .y_label_area_size(45)\n        .build_cartesian_2d(min_x..max_x, min_y..max_y)\n        .unwrap();\n\n    chart.configure_mesh()\n        .label_style((\"sans-serif\", 12).into_font().color(&RGBColor(180, 180, 180)))\n        .axis_style(RGBColor(60, 60, 80))\n        .draw()\n        .unwrap();\n\n    // Draw orbital trails as colored lines\n    for (i, traj) in histories.iter().enumerate() {\n        let color = colors[i % colors.len()];\n        chart.draw_series(LineSeries::new(\n            traj.iter().copied(),\n            color,\n        ))\n        .unwrap()\n        .label(labels[i % labels.len()])\n        .legend(move |(lx, ly)| {\n            Rectangle::new([(lx, ly - 4), (lx + 12, ly + 4)], color.filled())\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Draw current positions as dots (larger for the star)\n    for (i, traj) in histories.iter().enumerate() {\n        if let Some(&(px, py)) = traj.last() {\n            let size = if i == 0 { 8 } else { 4 };\n            let color = colors[i % colors.len()];\n            chart.draw_series(std::iter::once(\n                Circle::new((px, py), size, color.filled()),\n            ))\n            .unwrap();\n        }\n    }\n\n    chart\n        .configure_series_labels()\n        .background_style(RGBColor(30, 30, 45).mix(0.9))\n        .label_font((\"sans-serif\", 13).into_font().color(&WHITE))\n        .border_style(RGBColor(80, 80, 100))\n        .draw()\n        .unwrap();\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Svg\":\"<svg width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 800 800\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\">\\n<rect x=\\\"0\\\" y=\\\"0\\\" width=\\\"800\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" opacity=\\\"1\\\" fill=\\\"#0F0F19\\\" stroke=\\\"none\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"400\\\" y=\\\"20\\\" dy=\\\"0.76em\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-family=\\\"sans-serif\\\" font-size=\\\"17.741935483870968\\\" opacity=\\\"1\\\" fill=\\\"#FFFFFF\\\">\\nN-Body Orbital Trails\\n</text>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"61\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"61\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"71\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"71\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"81\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"81\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"91\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"91\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"101\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"101\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"111\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"111\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"121\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"121\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"131\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"131\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"141\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"141\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"151\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"151\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"161\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"161\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"171\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"171\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"181\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"181\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"192\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"192\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"202\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"202\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"212\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"212\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"222\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"222\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"232\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"232\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"242\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"242\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"252\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"252\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"262\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"262\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"272\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"272\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"282\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"282\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"292\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"292\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"302\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"302\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>\\n<line opacity=\\\"0.1\\\" stroke=\\\"#000000\\\" stroke-width=\\\"1\\\" x1=\\\"312\\\" y1=\\\"749\\\" x2=\\\"312\\\" y2=\\\"50\\\"/>